From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VectraOS port <port@vectraos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:53:10 -0600
Subject: [VectraOS] Read models without assimp

A small loader for the formats vkmark's scenes and tests use: 3DS (cube,
cat, horse), PLY (kmscube; ASCII and binary) and OBJ (the tests' strings).
Each gives triangles as assimp's Triangulate, SortByPType, GenNormals and
JoinIdenticalVertices steps left them for to_mesh: polygons as fans from
their first corner, lines and points dropped, a 3DS mesh in its local space
(the inverse of its mesh matrix, x negated where it mirrors) with normals
summed over the triangles that share a corner's position and a smoothing
group, and a flat normal for each triangle of a PLY or OBJ model without
its own. tests/model_test.cpp passes unchanged.
